<title>UK: BADMINTON-ALL ENGLAND CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BADMINTON-ALL ENGLAND CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, England 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the</p>
<p>All England badminton championships on Wednesday (prefix number</p>
<p>denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Men's singles, second round</p>
<p>5/8-Budi Santosa (Indonesia) beat Thomas Sogaard (Denmark) 15-5</p>
<p>15-12</p>
<p>Martin Lundgaard-Hansen (Denmark) beat 9-16-Chen Gang (China)</p>
<p>11-15 15-11 17-15</p>
<p>5/8-Ong Ewe Hock (Malaysia) beat Oliver Pongratz (Germany) 15-5</p>
<p>15-2</p>
<p>9/16-Dong Jiong (China) beat Kenneth Jonassen (Denmark) 15-9</p>
<p>15-1</p>
<p>Lin Liwen (China) beat Yong Hock Kin (Malaysia) 15-12 15-10</p>
<p>5/8-Indra Wijaya (Indonesia) beat Kasper Odum (Denmark) 15-5</p>
<p>15-6</p>
<p>P.Gopi Chand (India) beat Vladislav Druzhchenko (Ukraine) 8-15</p>
<p>15-11 18-14</p>
<p>Luo Yigang (China) beat Jesper Olsson 15-8 15-3</p>
<p>9/16-Heryanto Arbi (Indonesia) beat Mark Constable (England)</p>
<p>10-15 15-10 15-9</p>
<p>2-Rashid Sidek (Malaysia) beat Iain Sydie (Canada) 15-10 15-11</p>
<p>1-Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen (Denmark) beat Xie Yangchun (China)</p>
<p>15-2 15-8</p>
<p>Pang Chen (Malaysia) beat 9/16-Hwang Sun-Ho (South Korea) 15-1</p>
<p>8-15 15-6</p>
<p>Peter Rasmussen (Den) beat 3/4-Joko Suprianto (Indonesia) 15-10</p>
<p>15-3</p>
<p>Thomas Johansson (Sweden) beat Colin Haughton (England) 15-8</p>
<p>15-2</p>
<p>9/16-Salim (Indonesia) beat Anders Boesen (Denmark)</p>
<p>16-18 15-12 18-17</p>
<p>3/4-Sun Jun (China) beat Peter Knowles (England) 15-9 15-2</p>
<p>Women's singles, second round</p>
<p>5/8-Kim Ji-hyun (South Korea) beat Yasuko Mizui (Japan) 11-5</p>
<p>11-7</p>
<p>Yao Yan (China) beat Michelle Rasmussen (Den) 11-0 11-1</p>
<p>Ra Kyung-min (South Korea) beat Mette Sorensen (Denmark) 11-6</p>
<p>11-6</p>
<p>5/8-Wang Chen (China) beat Colhako Nakayama (Japan) 12-9 11-1</p>
<p>1-Mia Audina (Indonesia) beat Hisako Mizui (Japan) 11-5 11-1</p>
<p>5/8-Suzi Susanti (Indonesia) beat Emma Chaffin (England) 11-1</p>
<p>11-1</p>
<p>Lee Joo-Hyun (South Korea) beat Takako Ida (Japan) 12-10 8-11</p>
<p>12-9</p>
<p>2-Gong Zhichao (China) beat V Tcherniavskaia (Belarus) 11-5</p>
<p>11-2</p>
<p>Dai Yun (China) beat Choi Ma-ree (South Korea) 11-1 12-10</p>
<p>5/8-Zhang Ning (China) beat Lee Soon-deuk (South Korea) 11-7</p>
<p>11-1</p>
<p>Marina Andrievskaya (Sweden) beat Pornsawan Plungwech</p>
<p>(Thailand) 12-10 11-4</p>
<p>3/4-Ya Zhaoying (China) beat Anne Sondergaard (Denmark) 11-1</p>
<p>11-0</p>
<p>Kanako Yonekura (Japan) beat Jo Muggeridge (England)</p>
<p>11-7 11-4</p>
<p>Han Jingna (China) beat Kelly Morgan (Wales) 11-4 11-7</p>
<p>3/4-Camilla Martin (Denmark) beat Margit Borg (Sweden) 11-6 11-5</p>
<p>Park Jin-Hyun (South Korea) beat Jaw Hua-Ching (Thailand) 11-2</p>
<p>11-1</p>
<p>Men's singles:</p>
<p>1-Poul-Erik Hoyer-Larsen (Denmark) beat Pang Chen (Malaysia) 15-7 18-15</p>
